backend mein Error Handling ka matlab hai agar API mein koi error aaye, toh server
crash hone ke bajaye proper error response bheje.
1. Normal error handling
app.get("/users", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const users = await getUsers();
    res.json(users);
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({
      message: "Server error",
    });
  }
});

2. Global Error Middleware
const errorMiddleware = (err, req, res, next) => {
  const statusCode = err.statusCode || 500;
  res.status(statusCode).json({
    success: false,
    message: err.message || "Internal Server Error",
  });
};
module.exports = errorMiddleware;

3. next(error) kya karta hai?
const express = require("express");
const app = express();
app.get("/users", (req, res, next) => {
  const error = new Error("Users not found");
  error.statusCode = 404;
  next(error);
});
// Error-handling middleware
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(err.statusCode || 500).json({
    message: err.message,
  });
});

4. Common HTTP error codes
Code	Meaning
400	Bad Request — invalid input
401	Unauthorized — login/authentication required
403	Forbidden — permission nahi
404	Resource nahi mila
500	Internal Server Error